{
 "name": "kof_basics",
 "title": "KOF basics (DOA6 Kasumi, Stellar Blade Eve, UFE 2 Robot Kyle)",
 "note": "The basics of the side-view fight (FightGame.basics), one pack for every fighter, for what a character's own game has no clip for: crouch, standing and crouching guard and their block-stun from Dead or Alive 6's Kasumi (KAS00001, 00284/00357, 00285/00359; her back dash KAS00010); the jump (take-off, rise, fall, landing), the roll (her forward evade) and the hit in the air from Stellar Blade's Eve (Proto_Lockon_Jump_Start/_End, Proto_Fall_Battle, Proto_Lockon_Evade_Forward, Result_Hit_Air_Light_Fall_Bw; 'clip@from-to' keeps that part); the rest - hit while crouching, a low hit, swept, knocked flying, falling down, getting up, the throw pair, the crouching and jumping strikes, the C+D blowback attack (WallLauncher) and the throw's grab - from UFE 2's Robot Kyle. Each fighter keeps her own standing A-D, skills, hurt, fall, lying and (if she has them) her own versions of these (tools/doa/*.json game clips, her strike pack's roles). Hit windows of Kyle's strikes are UFE's active frames (60 per second, after the speed): frame f = f x speed / 60 s (_work/ufe2/ufe_moves.tsv).",
